{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5sz74qacpmenpyclky3lan5ndn2kzs6qgn45gabfpq3qhpxixpwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The library was small (a single translation unit), so I translated it directly rather than delegating.\n\n## What was in `c_src/`\n- `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` — globs `src/lib.c` into one SHARED library\n- `c_src/include/lib.h` — declares only `fallcalc`, no namespace/rename macros\n- `c_src/src/lib.c` — 176 lines, 6 non-static (hence exported) functions\n\n## Symbol-list verification (the completion gate)\nBuilt the C `.so` with gcc and diffed `nm -D` output against my Rust `.so`:\n\n| C export | Rust export |\n|---|---|\n| `allocate_and_compute` | ✅ |\n| `fallcalc` | ✅ |\n| `foreach_sum` | ✅ |\n| `process_array_reverse` | ✅ |\n| `safe_double_to_int` | ✅ |\n| `switch_fallthrough_calculator` | ✅ |\n\n`comm -23 c.syms rust.names` → **empty diff**. All 6/6 covered.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n- **Switch fall-through** (`switch_fallthrough_calculator`): cases 0→1→2 and 3→4 fall through with no `break`. Each Rust match arm replays the full downstream operation chain rather than just its own statement.\n- **`FOREACH` macro** expansion in `foreach_sum` — expanded to the equivalent index loop.\n- **Backwards pointer walk** in `process_array_reverse` (decrements from `end`), kept as raw-pointer arithmetic.\n- **`malloc`/`free` are the real libc ones**, declared `extern \"C\"`, not Rust's allocator. This matters: `size * sizeof(DataPoint)` converts `int`→`size_t` *before* multiplying, so a negative `size` (reachable via `fallcalc`'s `param4 % 10 + 1` when `param4` is negative) wraps to a ~2^64 request that fails and returns `-1`. It also preserves glibc's non-NULL `malloc(0)`. Rust's `alloc` would not behave the same.\n- **Wrapping integer arithmetic** everywhere C signed overflow is reachable, so release-mode Rust doesn't panic where C silently wraps.\n- **`safe_double_to_int` check order** kept exactly: NaN → inf → `>= INT_MAX` → `<= INT_MIN` → truncating cast.\n- **Float expression grouping** kept verbatim; on baseline x86-64 (SSE2, no FMA) gcc cannot contract these into `fma`, so results are bit-identical.\n- `#[repr(C)]` on `DataPoint` for the 16-byte layout.\n\n## Differential test\nWrote a `dlopen` harness loading both `.so`s side by side and comparing all 6 functions, including edge cases: `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` inputs, negative operands to `%`, NaN/±inf/±0.0, values straddling `2147483647.0`, negative and zero array counts, and `allocate_and_compute` with sizes from `-100000` to `INT_MAX`.\n\n**715,946 comparisons, 0 mismatches.**\n\n`cargo build --release` compiles clean, `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]` is set, and nothing in `c_src/` was touched (verified: 0 files modified).\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the CMake project name derives from the *parent directory* of `c_src`, which in this checkout is `translated_rust` — so the C build would emit `libtranslated_rust.so`, whereas mine is `libc_src.so`. Since only one `.so` exists in `target/release/`, a glob-based harness will find it, but tell me if your test loads a specific filename and I'll rename the crate lib to match."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":915,"cache_read_input_tokens":31433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":915,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"91a4cea4-4ce5-4708-bb3c-ed9a2d730e9c","uuid":"efe2e7a0-630a-418c-92d2-e3a0054b0b16","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:18:14.094Z"}
